---Describes options for object rewrite.
---@class gcp.storagebatchoperations_v1.RewriteObject
---@field kmsKey? string Optional. Resource name of the Cloud KMS key that is used to encrypt the object. The Cloud KMS key must be located in same location as the object. For details, see https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/encryption/using-customer-managed-keys#add-object-key Format: `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}/keyRings/{keyring}/cryptoKeys/{key}` For example: `projects/123456/locations/us-central1/keyRings/my-keyring/cryptoKeys/my-key`. The object will be rewritten and set with the specified KMS key.
---@field storageClass? gcp.storagebatchoperations_v1.RewriteObjectStorageClassEnum|string Optional. Rewrites the object to the specified storage class. Setting this field will perform a full byte copy of the object if the storage class is different from the object's current storage class. If Autoclass is enabled on the bucket, storage class changes are ignored by Cloud Storage.

---@alias gcp.storagebatchoperations_v1.RewriteObjectStorageClassEnum "STORAGE_CLASS_UNSPECIFIED"|"STANDARD"|"NEARLINE"|"COLDLINE"|"ARCHIVE"

